      "name": "Release a draft for public comment",
      "summary": "The whole public comment cycle around the comments themselves.",
      "description": "The whole public comment cycle around the comments themselves. The\ncommittee and editor agree a release date; the draft is frozen as a\npublic comment release with fixed line numbers (a PDF and a permanent\nPC/<version> site); the editor sets up every channel against that\nrelease, with instructions and links, and writes the announcement; the\npublic is told; comments come back and are handled one by one in\nProcess_PublicComment; and the release is archived with the review.\nCalled from Process_Publication. Skills: public-comment, document-publishing.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
